From 43c6616e69aefcaab0285c700d8cbe844a59c4b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nishil Faldu <faldund@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 01:22:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf(streamdown): repair only the end of a streaming message

On every streaming update, Streamdown ran remend over the whole message
and ran three regex checks (footnote references, footnote definitions,
link definitions) over the whole message. The work per update grew with
the length of the answer.

Each message now keeps a stable length: the end of every block except
the last two, taken from an update where remend changed nothing. Later
updates repair only the text after it. The three checks keep their
previous result and scan only where a new match can end.

The output equals a full repair because remend now completes syntax
only in the current block (#670 for emphasis, #685 for links).
